f up to  him when  when he's ready to compete which that  doesn't mean he tells me that doesn't  mean  i tell him hey we'll all see it and i  think it'll start with me but i'll go to  the coaches i'll go to the players and  um guys know when a guy's ready to  compete with a starter  and you kind of get that vibe and as  soon as as soon as it's like that i will  let them compete but i'm not really  setting a date on it because  i know how hard that'll be so how much  did your dad  uh play a role in you you grinded tape  and  talking and evaluating uh lance you know  word is and i know that there was lots  of word as you heard mac jones was the  initial  uh thought amongst the uh major media  outlets to be your choice  um how much was your dad involved in all  of this  um my dad was involved the same way he  is every off season  um which is i you know i bet every coach  talks to their parents  a little bit yeah give their opinions um  my  my my dad actually his opinion i think  is pretty good so i think i might listen  to it or take it in a little bit more  than most  people um but that's really about it  whether it's a quarterback or anything  it's  without saying in my press conference  the the whole um  that this is a shanahan's decision it's  it's somewhat comical i mean i kind of  laugh at it a little bit but then  i feel bad that that's insulting to  other people in our building because  that isn't the case my dad  i think everyone here loves when my dad  comes he  comes for a few weeks every april does  the same thing in the draft every year  just sits in there with us watches it  rarely talks when people ask them  questions they'll answer  but i love having them around really  cool to  be able to watch tape with your dad  someone who got out of football a little  bit  early i think who still mind works and  still loves to look at it  i mean with the way technology is right  now i mean my dad loves watching all our  practices he watches the individual  stuff that's  i won't get around to some of the more  boring stuff and he'll call me a month  later and be like hey did you see that  drill that  chris eric did and d-lineman play and  i'm like dad why aren't you at the beach  like why the hell are you watching him  d-line individual drill right now  and it's he enjoys it and um i think  it's pretty cool for him pretty cool for  me and  something i'll never stop doing as long  as he wants to do it  well the reason why i knew that you  really liked trey lance is you didn't  choose another quarterback in the fourth  round kyle  so uh you know i saw that  that's so funny with that stuff too  because and that back to that story i  remember  um you know we were taking rg3 kirk was  the guy i had ranked as a hyatt guy  that before we made that trade i thought  we i wanted to take him in the second  round  and before we my dad loved russell  wilson and he planned on taking russell  on the force  um and then when we took uh robert he  told me all along if russell was there  in the fourth he was going to take him  and then russell i don't know if he went  in the third or the fourth but he went  before  so i thought that was gone and then we  were sitting there on the clock  my dad goes i'm gonna take cousins and i  was like dad why the hell are you taking  cousins  we're going we're going this direction  and he's like because you had him  rank's so high we love him as a player  and russell's not there  i was like hey i'm not going to say no  to that go ahead and take them  but um i think they ended up being a  good decision but you don't always get  out of get to come out and explain  exactly why you did it  well uh before i let you go one other  hot uh rumor that was out there if you  wouldn't mind uh addressing  uh is that you know and and and the  difficulty of asking this question is i  don't want it at all to be  viewed as lance isn't your guy in any  way shape or form  but because i loved him when i spoke to  him last tuesday 